usage: calibrate.py [-h] [--prompts PROMPTS] [--count COUNT] [--res HxW]
                    [--scales SCALES] [--steps STEPS] [--guidance GUIDANCE]
                    [--seed SEED] [--sigma-bins SIGMA_BINS]
                    [--mu-mode {max_shift,default}] [--n0 N0] [--tile TILE]
                    [--window WINDOW] [--pool {center,mean}]
                    [--local-impl {flex,gather}] [--mass-queries MASS_QUERIES]
                    --out OUT [--report-only]
                    [--transfer-with [TRANSFER_WITH ...]] [--model {dev,krea}]
                    [--device DEVICE]

SCA calibration: run FLUX with exact attention at an in-distribution
resolution, emulate scales s_c (window n/s_c, pooling s_c), accumulate output-
matching statistics per prompt (resumable), then merge into a pi table npz and
a JSON report (same path, .json).

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --prompts PROMPTS
  --count COUNT
  --res HxW
  --scales SCALES
  --steps STEPS
  --guidance GUIDANCE
  --seed SEED
  --sigma-bins SIGMA_BINS
  --mu-mode {max_shift,default}
  --n0 N0
  --tile TILE           Inference tile t; emulation uses t * Wc / Wn
  --window WINDOW       Inference window Wn (default n0)
  --pool {center,mean}
  --local-impl {flex,gather}
                        Local branch implementation (same keys; flex uses a
                        FlexAttention block mask)
  --mass-queries MASS_QUERIES
  --out OUT             pi table .npz; parts go to <out stem>_parts/
  --report-only         Merge existing parts without running FLUX
  --transfer-with [TRANSFER_WITH ...]
                        Other calibration npz files
  --model {dev,krea}    dev = FLUX.1-dev; krea = FLUX.1-Krea-dev transformer
                        with FLUX.1-dev encoders and VAE
  --device DEVICE
